# Minimal RDF test dataset for QLever integration tests.
# Contains scientists with basic properties for predictable query results.

# --- Types ---
<http://example.org/Albert_Einstein> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Scientist> .
<http://example.org/Marie_Curie> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Scientist> .
<http://example.org/Isaac_Newton> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Scientist> .
<http://example.org/Ada_Lovelace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Mathematician> .
<http://example.org/Nikola_Tesla> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Inventor> .
<http://example.org/Physics> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Field> .
<http://example.org/Chemistry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Field> .
<http://example.org/Mathematics> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Field> .
<http://example.org/Engineering> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/Field> .

